---
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/one-frame-blue-threshold-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/one-frame-blue-threshold-dark.svg?raw';
import Chart from './Chart.astro';
---

<Chart
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  title="The blue cutoff sits just above steel blue, at 160"
  caption="signalstats ULOW per frame, TV-range decode. Real content, the VCR channel screen and the tape leader are readings from two real tapes; the solid colors are synthetic test frames."
>
  Dot chart of ULOW readings on a 0 to 255 scale with the production cutoff at 160 and the first cutoff at 180. Kept,
  below 160: real content at 36 to 114, gray or black at 128, sky blue at 151, steel blue at 159. Dropped, at 160 or
  above: purple at 165, cyan at 166, a VCR channel screen at 166 to 167, navy at 184, magenta at 202, a saturated tape
  leader at 217 to 218, pure blue at 240. Purple, cyan and the VCR channel screen sit between 160 and 180, so the
  first cutoff kept them.
</Chart>
